  "answer": "⚠️ Out of distribution: O2 21% outside the tested range for PMMA rod (14.5–20.8%)\nTreat every number below as an extrapolation, not a validated prediction.\n\n**Assumptions**\n- No material specified: showing every material in the model.\n- No atmosphere specified: assuming the ISS cabin preset.\n\n**Verdict**\n**SIBAL fabric is FLAMMABLE** at 21% O2 for modeled flows from 3 to 30 cm/s.\n**PMMA film is FLAMMABLE** at 21% O2 for modeled flows from 1 to 10 cm/s.\n**PMMA slab is FLAMMABLE** at 21% O2 for modeled flows from 2 to 20 cm/s.\n**No verdict for PMMA rod at 21% O2**: every modeled flow is outside or far from the labelled NASA data.\n**Nomex is not flammable at any modeled flow**: P(burn) < 0.5 at 21% O2 at every modeled flow inside its data.\n\n**Key numbers**\n- At 8 cm/s, P(burn) is already ≥ 0.5 at the lowest modeled O2 (16.4%).\n- At 1 cm/s, P(burn) is already ≥ 0.5 at the lowest modeled O2 (17.3%).\n- Lowest O2 where P(burn) ≥ 0.5 for PMMA slab: 17% at 2 cm/s, 14.7 psia.\n- At 1 cm/s, P(burn) is already ≥ 0.5 at the lowest modeled O2 (14.5%).\n\n**Evidence**\n- GMT96-T7 (T'ien, Table 7.1/A.6, p. 95; SIBAL fabric, 21% O2, 14.7 psia, 10 cm/s) → burn\n- GMT96-T8 (T'ien, Table 7.1/A.6, p. 95; SIBAL fabric, 21% O2, 14.7 psia, 5 cm/s) → burn\n- GMT100-T5 (T'ien, Table 7.1/A.6, p. 113; SIBAL fabric, 18.8% O2, 14.7 psia, 2.4 cm/s) → burn\n\n**Operational recommendation**\n- Do not use this output for a go/no-go decision; it is outside the validated data. Apply the most conservative material controls and request testing.\n- Treat the material as flammable in this atmosphere: minimize exposed quantity and keep it away from ignition sources.\n\n**Limits**\n- Model scope: the five BASS-II materials (SIBAL fabric, PMMA film, PMMA slab, PMMA rod, Nomex), ISS microgravity at 1 atm only (NASA/TM-20210011385); spread rate only for PMMA slabs (Table 5.1).\n- Decision support only, not a replacement for NASA-STD-6001 material testing.",
